policy_id: jp-copyright-article-30-4
version: 0.1.2
jurisdiction: JP
legal_basis: Japan Copyright Act Article 30-4
source_reviewed_at: 2026-09-13
purpose: >-
  Route a proposed use of a work through a narrow, auditable Article 30-4
  profile. This policy does not determine overall legality and does not discover
  or prove the actual training data of a specific AI model.

decisions:
  AUTO: supplied facts satisfy this profile or Article 30-4 is out of scope
  REVIEW: a material fact or legal characterization is unresolved
  DENY: this profile cannot authorize under Article 30-4 on supplied facts

statutory_layers:
  - id: non_enjoyment
    description: >-
      The use must not have a purpose of enjoying the ideas or emotions expressed
      in the target work. A coexisting enjoyment purpose means this layer is not met.
    subchecks:
      - enjoyment_of_target_work == false
      - intentional_reproduction_output_purpose != true
      - coexisting_enjoyment_purpose == false
    evidence_signals:
      - incidental_similar_output_observed_is_not_dispositive
      - frequent_common_expression_outputs_may_require_review
      - user_prompt_attribution_can_negate_that_frequency_inference
  - id: necessary_extent
    test: within_necessary_extent == true
  - id: no_unreasonable_prejudice
    test: unreasonably_prejudices_rightsholder == false

notes:
  - information_analysis_is_example_not_exclusive_requirement
  - deny_does_not_mean_unlawful_other_bases_may_apply
  - source_legality_contract_privacy_and_other_laws_are_out_of_scope
  - known_pirated_source_is_recorded_as_a_signal_not_a_standalone_statutory_element
  - intentional_reproduction_output_purpose_concerns_protected_creative_expression_not_style_as_such
  - isolated_similar_output_alone_does_not_establish_training_stage_enjoyment_purpose
  - marked_frequency_of_common_creative_expression_outputs_can_trigger_review_as_indirect_evidence
  - user_prompt_caused_frequency_does_not_itself_support_trainer_enjoyment_purpose
  - provenance_is_preserved_but_not_independently_verified_by_this_gate

official_sources:
  - title: AI and Copyright
    publisher: Agency for Cultural Affairs
    url: https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/chosakuken/aiandcopyright.html
  - title: Approach to AI and Copyright
    date: 2024-03-15
    publisher: Copyright Subdivision, Cultural Council, Agency for Cultural Affairs
    url: https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/bunkashingikai/chosakuken/pdf/94037901_01.pdf
  - title: FAQ on legal issues in cultural and artistic activities
    publisher: Agency for Cultural Affairs
    url: https://www.bunka.go.jp/seisaku/bunka_gyosei/kibankyoka/faq/index.html

changelog:
  - version: 0.1.2
    change: >-
      Reframed the policy as three statutory layers, with coexisting enjoyment
      purpose treated as part of the non-enjoyment layer. Removed misleading
      style-reproduction wording and tied the specific signal to
      output of protected creative expression. Added marked-frequency and
      user-prompt-attribution signals from the Agency's p.21 discussion, routing
      unresolved/non-user-attributed marked frequency to REVIEW. Added an optional
      provenance manifest preserved in receipts and an explicit non-goal that this
      gate does not discover or prove any model's actual training data.
  - version: 0.1.1
    change: >-
      Split the coexisting-enjoyment check into a specific
      intentional_reproduction_output_purpose signal and a general/manual fallback.
      Added incidental_similar_output_observed as informational-only context.
